gaps.remedy:
In `game/src/render/water.js`, replace the fixed floor with a Schlick Fresnel over the SAME `esView` the file already computes, so the distance term broadens the grazing response instead of adding a floor under it:
    float esF0 = 0.02;
    float esRefl = esF0 + (1.0 - esF0) * pow(1.0 - esView, 5.0);
    esRefl = max(esRefl, smoothstep(10.0, 52.0, length(vViewPosition)) * 0.72 * (1.0 - esView));
    vec3 esSurface = mix(esDepth, esReflection, esRefl * uWaterReflectionStrength);
DONE means all four of these, and the fourth is the S59 preservation clause naming what must not get worse:
(a) the composited reflection weight straight down at 120 m is <= 0.05, and at the 60 m grazing marsh vista is >= 0.60, read off the same probe the build used;
(b) RI-VIS03 M12 `FresnelDelta` at a `water_edge` shot is >= 0.05 and POSITIVE — it is -0.07790 today (`node tools/visual/f7-critic-m12-offline.mjs`);
(c) `lane_power_normalised` on the water mask at vista-deep-marshes falls by >= 40% against b0f3224e's 0.000485 (`node tools/visual/f7-critic-reanalyse.mjs`), reported ALONGSIDE mean_luma so a darkening cannot be read as a de-streaking again;
(d) PRESERVATION — mean luminance on the water mask does not fall below 70 (it is 84.961 today, down from 102.223 pre-fix), the grazing-pose composite weight does not fall, and M12 `ShoreDelta` stays >= 0.03. Without (d) this remedy can be 'passed' by making the water black, which is the same shape of failure as the one being fixed.
